    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108038" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπην-ήτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one that is just getting a beard</i> (cf. foreg.),
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῶτον ὑ.</span> a youth <i>with
			his</i> first <i>beard,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.348
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.279
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				309b
			</span></i> (quoting Homer), <i><span class="en">
				Him.
				<u>Ecl.</u>
				13.24
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑρμῆς ὑ.,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεὺς γενειήτης,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Sacr.</u>
				11
			</span></i>: generally, <i>bearded,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.32
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>).</div>
